! Surfaces: the areas of the polygons reproduce the xlsx areas of raw_data columns F, J and K.
! Dimensions used in the vertex comments: W = 163.75 ft and D = 109.17 ft (W / 1.5): NREL PDF Table 13, Medium Office, 53,628 ft2, 3 floors, aspect ratio 1.5, so the plate is 53,628 / 3 = 17,876 ft2 and W = sqrt(17,876 x 1.5) = 163.7 ft (the prototype writes 163.75 ft); H = 13 ft: floor-to-floor height (PDF Table 13); d = 15 ft: depth of the perimeter zones and c = 9 ft: ceiling height of the zones, so that each plenum is H - c = 4 ft (dimensions of the prototype, not in the documents).
  BuildingSurface:Detailed,
    Building_Roof,                !- Name
    Roof,                         !- Surface Type
    Roof,                         !- Construction Name
    TopFloor_Plenum,              !- Zone Name
    ,                             !- Space Name
    Outdoors,                     !- Outside Boundary Condition
    ,                             !- Outside Boundary Condition Object
    ,                             !- Sun Exposure
    ,                             !- Wind Exposure
    ,                             !- View Factor to Ground
    ,                             !- Number of Vertices
    49.911,0,11.8872,             !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 1 {m}  Derived from: X = W = 163.75 ft x 0.3048 = 49.911 m; Y = 0 (zone origin); Z = 3 H = 3 x 3.9624 = 11.8872 m (H = 13 ft x 0.3048).
    49.911,33.2738,11.8872,       !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 2 {m}  Derived from: X = W = 163.75 ft x 0.3048 = 49.911 m; Y = D = 109.17 ft x 0.3048 = 33.2740 m (the prototype value is 33.2738, the formula gives 33.2740); Z = 3 H = 3 x 3.9624 = 11.8872 m (H = 13 ft x 0.3048).
    0,33.2738,11.8872,            !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 3 {m}  Derived from: X = 0 (zone origin); Y = D = 109.17 ft x 0.3048 = 33.2740 m (the prototype value is 33.2738, the formula gives 33.2740); Z = 3 H = 3 x 3.9624 = 11.8872 m (H = 13 ft x 0.3048).
